  "description": {
    "format": "nuke_help_html",
    "plain_text": "Run Python code on the incoming stage. The USD stage and edit layer can be accessed through these methods on the variable \"geo_python\": geo_python.stage() - the USD stage. geo_python.layer() - the USD edit layer. Other useful methods: geo_python.name() - the name of the node. geo_python.fullName() - the full name of the node. geo_python.knob(name) - a handle to a user knob. geo_python.setModifiedPaths(paths) - set the list of paths that this node modifies. geo_python.setCreatedPaths(paths) - set the list of paths that this node creates. You may author changes to the stage using the high-level APIs or the layer using low-level APIs, but not both. The stage's edit target is set to the edit layer. Do not change it or you will get undefined behaviour. Console output appears in the Script Editor panel. Use geo_python.knob() to access any user knobs on the node. This returns an object you can call getValue() on to safely get the value of the knob (accessing knobs directly while running a node is not supported). You can also call isAnimated() to determine if the knob animates, which can be useful when deciding to generate time samples or not. A list of requested times is provided by geo_python.times(). Your code should generate time samples for each of these times for any animated attributes.",
    "source": "nuke.Node.help()",
    "text": "Run Python code on the incoming stage.\n\nThe USD stage and edit layer can be accessed through these methods on the variable \"geo_python\":\n\n  geo_python.stage() - the USD stage.\n  geo_python.layer() - the USD edit layer.\n\nOther useful methods:\n  geo_python.name() - the name of the node.\n  geo_python.fullName() - the full name of the node.\n  geo_python.knob(name) - a handle to a user knob.\n  geo_python.setModifiedPaths(paths) - set the list of paths that this node modifies.\n  geo_python.setCreatedPaths(paths) - set the list of paths that this node creates.\n\nYou may author changes to the stage using the high-level APIs or the layer\nusing low-level APIs, but not both.\n\nThe stage's edit target is set to the edit layer. Do not change it or you will get\nundefined behaviour.\n\nConsole output appears in the Script Editor panel.\n\nUse geo_python.knob() to access any user knobs on the node. This returns an object you can \ncall getValue() on to safely get the value of the knob (accessing knobs directly while running\na node is not supported). You can also call isAnimated() to determine if the knob animates,\nwhich can be useful when deciding to generate time samples or not.\n\nA list of requested times is provided by geo_python.times(). Your code should generate time\nsamples for each of these times for any animated attributes.\n"
  },
